---
import {
  ArrowRight,
  ArrowUpRight,
  SlidersHorizontal,
  ScanSearch,
} from '@lucide/astro';
import CodeWindow from './CodeWindow.astro';
import Tabs from './Tabs.astro';
import examples from '../data/examples.json';

const guide = 'https://kedi-lang.org/docs/agent-adapters/typesafe/';
---

<section id="jev" class="section jev-section" aria-labelledby="jev-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-kicker">
      <span>05 / KEDI + JEV</span>
      <a class="jev-maker" href="https://typesafe.ai/">
        JEV BY TYPESAFE <ArrowUpRight size={13} />
      </a>
    </div>
    <h2 id="jev-title">
      Typed judgments.
      <br />
      Your next move.
    </h2>
    <p class="section-intro">
      Choose a route, score urgency, or assess a draft. Jev returns typed
      judgments; your Kedi program decides what happens next.
    </p>
    <dl class="jev-primitives" aria-label="Jev primitives in Kedi">
      <div>
        <dt>Score</dt>
        <dd>
          Grade against your own <code>Rubric</code>. Describe the ordered
          levels; receive a numeric score, not a paragraph to parse.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Choice</dt>
        <dd>
          Select from <code>Literal</code> or enum options. Add{' '}
          <code>ChoiceCriteria</code> to define what each option means.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Probability</dt>
        <dd>
          Keep the raw assessment as a <code>Probability</code>, a float between
          0 and 1. Your program decides how to act on it.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Criteria</dt>
        <dd>
          State what to evaluate in <code>Annotated</code>. Use{' '}
          <code>BooleanCriteria</code> to describe positive and negative
          evidence.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <Tabs
      id="jev-examples"
      label="Jev workflow examples"
      tabs={[
        { id: 'routing', label: 'Assess & route' },
        { id: 'review', label: 'Draft & review' },
      ]}
    >
      <div
        id="jev-examples-panel-routing"
        role="tabpanel"
        aria-labelledby="jev-examples-tab-routing"
        class="showcase-layout"
        data-panel="routing"
      >
        <CodeWindow example={examples.jevRouting} id="jev-routing" />
        <aside
          class="showcase-aside jev-aside"
          aria-label="Typed ticket routing"
        >
          <div class="decision-rule">
            <span class="tiny-label">AN ASSESSMENT THAT GOES SOMEWHERE</span>
            <p>
              <span>billing / priority</span>
            </p>
            <span class="decision-caption">
              A finite queue, a rubric score, and a raw probability become a
              routing decision.
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="jev-detail">
            <SlidersHorizontal size={21} aria-hidden="true" />
            <h3>Define what matters.</h3>
            <p>
              <code>ChoiceCriteria</code> describes the queues.{' '}
              <code>Rubric</code> defines three urgency levels, scored from 0 to
              2. <code>Probability</code> retains the cancellation assessment.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="jev-detail">
            <ScanSearch size={21} aria-hidden="true" />
            <h3>Make the rule explicit.</h3>
            <p>
              All three fields share one Jev request. The Python condition
              selects the priority lane locally, without another model call.
            </p>
          </div>
          <p class="aside-caption">
            Illustrative scores and example routing thresholds, not measured
            accuracy or a calibrated policy.
          </p>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <div
        id="jev-examples-panel-review"
        role="tabpanel"
        aria-labelledby="jev-examples-tab-review"
        class="showcase-layout"
        data-panel="review"
        hidden
      >
        <CodeWindow example={examples.jev} id="jev" />
        <aside
          class="showcase-aside jev-aside"
          aria-label="Jev decisions in Kedi"
        >
          <div class="decision-rule">
            <span class="tiny-label">YOUR POLICY, IN CODE</span>
            <p>
              <span>probability</span> <strong>&gt; 0.90</strong>
            </p>
            <span class="decision-caption">
              Only then does <code>approved</code> become true.
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="jev-detail">
            <SlidersHorizontal size={21} aria-hidden="true" />
            <h3>You set the bar.</h3>
            <p>
              Choose the threshold for the decision. A boolean isn't an
              unexplained yes or no.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="jev-detail">
            <ScanSearch size={21} aria-hidden="true" />
            <h3>Keep the evidence.</h3>
            <p>
              <code>decision_info</code> exposes the recorded probability and
              threshold without another model call.
            </p>
          </div>
          <p class="aside-caption">
            Illustrative values, not a measured run. A probability is not a
            correctness guarantee.
          </p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </Tabs>
    <a class="text-link jev-guide" href={guide}>
      Explore the Jev integration <ArrowRight size={17} />
    </a>
  </div>
</section>
